            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery disease: revascularization strategies for patients with CAD and diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>364-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nrcardio.2010.82</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>CABG surgery has been considered the optimal revascularization strategy for patients with diabetes mellitus who have lexft main and/or multivessel coronary artery disease. The results of a new analysis of data from the SYNTAX trial challenge this conventional wisdom and highlight additional coronary revascularization options to physicians and patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
